Third-party test fixtures
=========================

Everything under Tests/Fixtures/corpus/ is a `project.pbxproj` copied, byte for
byte, from an open-source project. Each file is pinned to a commit and is
distributed under that project's licence, whose text is kept under
Tests/Fixtures/licenses/. The files are test data only: nothing in them is
compiled into, or shipped with, pbxedit.

The files were fetched from raw.githubusercontent.com at the commit shown and
checked against the git blob hash GitHub reports for that path and commit.
`SHA-256` is the digest of the committed bytes; the corpus test fails if a file
no longer matches it. Do not edit these files: a corpus file that does not
round-trip is a parser bug, never a fixture to be adjusted.

Tests/Fixtures/handwritten/ is original to this repository and is not
third-party material.

